 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Night sky; Dawud, Isa and Maryam: no motif; two paths for «يتولون الذين كفروا» only. 78:7-12 «على لسان داود وعيسى» is not glossed: Al-Muyassar reads it as the Zabur and the Injil, As-Sa'di as their testimony. STAGING v4: 78-79: a town at dusk; three men (the disbelievers of Bani Israil) stand; Dawud and Isa appear only as blue labelled drops on their names (78:9, 78:10) and leave on 78:13; they do not speak (the tafsirs differ on how the curse came: the Zabur and the Injil, or their testimony), only shot_wide while they are on stage. The men turn away on 78:15 (disobedience); nobody is shown forbidding (79:3). 80-81: three men (many of them; two others of them stand still) walk to the idolaters on 80:4 and talk with them on 80:6 (taking them as allies); they stay on stage through the wrath and the punishment words; nothing is acted on the counterfactual of 81:1-11; the camera holds on them on 81:13 and they turn away on 81:15."
 },
